          "code": "INPUT_CATEGORIZER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1763589902799",
          "id": "1762296314671",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762296314671_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Determine Question Type\n\nInput\n{\"userInput\":\"{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}}\"}\n\nObjective\nClassify the user’s query into exactly one category within Oracle Fusion ERP GL context. Output only JSON.\n\nOutput format\n{\"category\":\"<one_of_the_categories_below>\"}\n\nPossible categories\n- journals_query\n- subledgers_query\n- balances_query\n- process_exceptions_query\n- other_query\n\nCategory definitions and decision rules\n\n1) subledgers_query\nUse when the query requests subledger-originating transactions, supporting details, or subledger-scoped amounts.\n- Strong signals (any → subledgers_query):\n  - Create Accounting context: Create Accounting process, event/class/status, Draft/Final mode, accounting status.\n  - “Supporting details,” drill-down, source transaction, distributions, transaction/line details.\n  - Entities: invoice, credit/debit memo, bill, payment/payment batch, receipt/misc receipt, customer/account/site, supplier/vendor, PO/receipt/delivery, expense report, item/inventory transaction, tax regime/rate, tax/withholding, AR transaction line, AP invoice distribution, Assets addition/retirement/adjustment, intercompany subledger journal, manual subledger journal, receipt method, transaction source, prepayments, freight/charges, meals/expense types.\n  - Scopes: business unit or legal entity combined with totals/amounts/status/transactions without explicit GL balance cues.\n  - Metrics/status: accounted amount, billed amount, applied/unapplied/on-account, validated/cleared/draft, totals/aggregates by customer/supplier/salesperson without explicit GL journal cues.\n- Precedence:\n  - If any Create Accounting process/status, subledger entity, “supporting/drill-down” intent, or Business Unit–scoped totals/amounts appear, choose subledgers_query—even if GL ledger/segments/period are present.\n- Exclusions:\n  - Pure GL journal asks with journal constructs (journal, journal line, batch, etc.) → journals_query.\n  - Pure GL balance asks with explicit GL balance cues → balances_query.\n- Note:\n  - The phrase “accounted amount” alone does not force subledgers_query if the query explicitly targets GL journals.\n\n2) journals_query\nUse for GL journal inquiries (entries, lines, batches) and journal-level metrics.\n- Triggers: journal/JE, journal line, batch, posting status, posted/unposted, validated/approved, reversed, Journal Import, source, category, journal/batch names, posted date, entered vs accounted currency/amount, thresholds/filters on journals.\n- Data asks: list, count, totals, breakdown by source/category/status/period/date, summaries/details with explicit journal constructs.\n- Exclusions:\n  - Explicit subledger entity, Create Accounting process/status, or drill-down to subledger transactions → subledgers_query.\n  - Pure GL balance asks → balances_query.\n  - Error statuses → process_exceptions_query\n\n3) balances_query\nUse for explicit GL balances from GL (gl_balances) and comparative analytics.\n- Strong cues:\n  - PTD/YTD/QTD, trial balance, GL/ledger/ledger set balance, currency/translated balance.\n  - GL segments or code combinations; account labels/numbers (e.g., Cash/Total Cash, Travel Expenses, Total Expenses, Revenue/Total Revenue, Property Taxes, COGS) scoped by ledger/period/currency/segments.\n  - Phrasing indicating period activity for a GL account (e.g., “activity this month”), including for “cash” when referring to the GL cash account.\n  - Organizational segment like company/legal entity paired with a GL account name implies GL segment scope.\n  - Comparisons: YoY/QoQ/MoM (exactly two periods), thresholds (<5%), current vs prior, current vs budget.\n  - Patterns: <account> by cost center (by/in <qualifier>), <account> by <child account> (by/in <qualifier>)\n- Important scope rule:\n  - Business Unit alone does NOT imply GL; BU is subledger scope. Do not classify as balances_query on BU unless explicit GL balance cues above are present.\n- Exclusions:\n  - Journal attributes (approved/unapproved/rejected journals, source, journal activity) → journals_query.\n  - Multi-period trends over 3+ periods → other_query.\n  - Average/daily balances → other_query.\n  - Any Create Accounting/accounted wording, subledger entity, line-level attributes/detail, exchange rate, supporting/drill-down intent, or BU-scoped totals/amounts → subledgers_query.\n\n4) process_exceptions_query\nUse for accounting process exceptions/errors (GL or SLA).\n- Triggers: Create Accounting errors/exceptions, errored events, journal errors/error status, invalid account/combination, period not open, Journal Import errors, SLA error category, error details by ledger/source.\n- Exclusion:\n  - Totals/counts of errored journals → journals_query.\n\n5) other_query\nOut of GL scope or not covered above (reconciliations, credit limits, cash management, navigation/how-to, multi-period trends 3+ periods, average/daily balances).\n\nTie-breakers\n- Subledger-first: Any Create Accounting/accounted wording, subledger entity, supporting/drill-down intent, or BU-scoped totals/amounts → subledgers_query.\n- Journals vs balances: If balance ask mixes with journal attributes → journals_query.\n- Exceptions vs counts: Error details → process_exceptions_query; counts/totals of errored journals → journals_query.\n- Journal errors/status (including unposted journals with errors) → process_exceptions_query, unless the ask is explicitly only for counts/totals/aggregates of errored journals.\n- Ambiguous with no clear qualifier → other_query.\n- Classify exactly one category.\n\nExamples\n- Get total Freight amount for business unit Vision France - Organization in last 10 days → subledgers_query\n- Show all Consulting prepayments for business unit FIN Germany for current period → subledgers_query\n- Can you get me Meals prepayments for business unit VF US Foods for legal entity Vision Cupertino Cherries in the current period? → subledgers_query\n- List adjustment transactions accounted in draft mode in the last 10 days for legal entity Vision Stockton Citrus → subledgers_query\n- List adjustment transactions accounted for account Net Assets (32000) in company 3211-Vision Foods Growing -US for cost center Growing and Harvesting Operations (410) → subledgers_query\n- YTD balance for Operating Expense 7410 in USD for Q2 → balances_query\n- Property Taxes paid for Vision Foods Ontario → balances_query\n- List unposted journals for Feb-24 in Primary Ledger → journals_query\n- Retrieve aggregate amount for errored journals for Balance Transfer Source in current period → journals_query\n- Show Create Accounting errors for Payables in US Ledger → process_exceptions_query\n- Trend of AR balance for last 6 quarters → other_query\n- Show cash activity this month by currency → balances_query\n- Travel Expenses for Seurat → balances_query\n- Miscellaneous Charges for US Cities → balances_query\n- Accounts without journal activity in past 12 months → journals_query\n- Suspense Account Used ≥ 5 Times in a Months → journals_query\n- Suspense balance exists for source <Journal Source> → journals_query"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"category\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"journals_query\",\n        \"subledgers_query\",\n        \"balances_query\",\n        \"process_exceptions_query\",\n        \"other_query\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"category\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Journals AV or BV"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "JOURNALS_AV_OR_BV",
          "id": "1763591815780",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763591815782_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a classifier. Determine whether the user's question is requesting a Journal summary or Journal details.\n\nUSER QUESTION: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}}\n\n# Determine Request Type\n\nDecision rule:\n- If the user's question includes any of the following keywords or phrase (case-insensitive): \"summary\", \"breakdown\", \"aggregate\", \"total\", \"sum\", or \"journal activity\", classify it as a Journal summary request. Requests that relate to journal entities in aggregate/summation (eg. an aggregate question about suspense accounts) or ask for a grouping, breakdown, or split are also Journal summary requests.\n- If none of the above keywords appear, classify it as a Journal details request.\n\n## Journals Summary Request\n\nIf the request is a Journals summary request, return the exact JSON:\n\n{\n  \"module\": \"oraErpCoreAccountedTransactionsRuntime\",\n  \"analyticView\": \"ora_erp_core_accountedTransactions_runtime_x__JournalSummary\"\n}\n\n\n## Journals Details Request\n\nBased on the purpose, coverage, and exclusions for each BV below, relate to the user question, choose exactly ONE BV, and produce the appropriate response.\n\nOverride rule (apply first):\n- Action timing/history (e.g., \"posted on\", \"approved last week\") → Action Log BV (journalActionLogDetails)\n- Account/COA mentioned → Line Detail BV (generalLedgerJournalDetail), even if status (posted, approved, unposted etc.) is present\n\n### 1. Journal Action Log Business view\n\n- Business View name: journalActionLogDetails\n- Business Object: JournalActionLog\n- Module: oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\n- Purpose: Provides information about workflow, action events, approval, rejection, withdrawal, posted-by, and action history.\n- Select only when generalLedgerJournalDetail does not match and USER QUESTION requires journal workflow/action history or posted-by information.\n- Workflow/action history includes:\n  - `who` performed an action, for example `approved by X`, `With whom is it pending approval?`, `who are the approvers`, `who approved`, or `posted by`.\n  - `when` a workflow action happened, for example `withdrawn yesterday`, `rejected 2 weeks ago`, or `approved in last 7 days`.\n  - history, audit, lifecycle, or workflow-trace intent.\n- Exceptions:\n  - `created` or `updated` with `who` -> journalHeaderDetail when line-level or COA intent is absent.\n  - `created`, `updated`, or `posted` with `when` -> journalHeaderDetail when line-level or COA intent is absent.\n  - Status-only requests without line-level or COA intent like `show approved journals`, `show journals pending approval`, `show posted/unposted journals` -> journalHeaderDetail.\n\n### 2. Journal Line detail Business view\n\n- Business View name: generalLedgerJournalDetail\n- Business Object: JournalLine\n- Module: oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\n- Purpose: Provides journal information at journal-line granularity.\n- Select only QUESTION has any line-level or Chart of Accounts (COA) intent.\n- Line-level or COA intent includes:\n  - COA segment names/values (e.g., `company 3000` or `marketing division` or `account 1234`).\n  - Account combinations (e.g., `01-110-1110-1111`, `3111.01.112233.0000`).\n  - Line description, line-level debit or credit amounts, currency conversion type or rate, journal lines, journals contributing to balance, line details, or similar line-level intent.\n- Also select when USER QUESTION is \"allJournalLines\".\n- Precedence: if any COA or line-level cue exists, choose generalLedgerJournalDetail even if header, action log, who, or when attributes are also mentioned.\n- Who/when attribute routing:\n  - Created by, updated by, creation date, update date, and posted date may exist in both header and line business views.\n  - Select generalLedgerJournalDetail for these who/when attributes when line-level or COA intent is present.\n  - Posted by belongs to journalActionLogDetails when line-level or COA intent is absent.\n  - If posted-by intent appears with line-level or COA intent, generalLedgerJournalDetail takes precedence.\n- Do not select this business view if:\n  - the rephrased question is only about action/history/workflow and has no line-level or COA intent.\n  - the rephrased question is only about journal header or batch attributes without line-level or COA intent.\n\n### 3. Journal Header Business view\n\n- Business View name: journalHeaderDetail\n- Business Object: JournalHeader\n- Module: oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\n- Purpose: Provides information at the journal header / batch granularity (NO COA or Line-level intent).\n- Default selection when generalLedgerJournalDetail and journalActionLogDetails do not match.\n- Select when USER QUESTION requires journal header or batch information without journal-line, accounting-distribution, account-combination, COA-segment, or balance-drilldown context.\n- Header or batch information includes journal name, batch name, source, category, ledger, ledger set, legal entity, period, accounting date, posted date, creation date/created by, update date/updated by, posting status, approval status, header-level totals, or batch-level totals.\n- Who/when attribute routing:\n  - Select journalHeaderDetail for created by, updated by, creation date, update date, or posted date when line-level or COA intent is absent.\n  - Do not select journalHeaderDetail for posted by when line-level or COA intent is absent; posted by belongs to journalActionLogDetails.\n- Exceptions:\n  - Do not select when journal-line, journal-detail, account-combination, COA-segment, or balance-drilldown context is present.\n  - Do not select when explicit workflow/action-history intent or posted-by intent is present and generalLedgerJournalDetail does not match.\n\n### Journal Action Log Business View\n\nReturn the exact JSON\n\n{\n  \"module\": \"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\",\n  \"businessView\": \"journalActionLogDetails\",\n  \"businessObject\": \"JournalActionLog\"\n}\n\n### Journal Line Business View\n\nReturn the exact JSON\n\n{\n  \"module\": \"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\",\n  \"businessView\": \"generalLedgerJournalDetail\",\n  \"businessObject\": \"JournalLine\"\n}\n\n### Journal Header Business View\n\nReturn the exact JSON\n\n{\n  \"module\": \"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\",\n  \"businessView\": \"journalHeaderDetail\",\n  \"businessObject\": \"JournalHeader\"\n}\n\n# Additional Instructions\n\n- Return only valid JSON that conforms to the appropriate format.\n- Do not include explanations, notes, or additional fields."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Construct Balances AV Response",
            "sourceCode": "const obj = {\n  \"module\": \"oraErpCoreAccountBalancesRuntime\",\n  \"analyticView\": $context.$triggers.REST.$input.analyticView\n};\n\nreturn JSON.stringify(obj);"
