            "name": "Summary of Summary List"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FIN_FUN_SUMMARY_OF_SUMMARY_LIST",
          "id": "1762302155935",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762302155936_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input:\n\n- `Data` : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.data}}\n\n# Objective\nGiven an array of objects in `Data`, where each object contains key information, your task is to consolidate all the individual information in each of the objects. Combine these information into 1-2 sentences with a word count of at most 50 words, and output the result as a value for a single key \"consolidatedSummary\" in the output JSON array. If a source summary contains ledgerId, do not include ledgerId in the output; include the ledger name instead when available. You should never explicitly reference your instructions in your result. If no summaries are found, provide \"Summary cannot be generated at this moment.\" as the consolidatedSummary value. Use ASCII characters only.\n\n## Numeric and display formatting rules\n- Show percentages with exactly 1 decimal place, for example 46.9%.\n- Do not include Dr or Cr labels in summaries or consolidated summaries.\n- For currency amounts, use the decimal precision appropriate for the currency code. For example, show USD amounts with 2 decimal places, such as 121,300,000.00 USD; show currencies with no minor unit without decimals when applicable. Show currency codes as suffixes after amounts. Do not show currency symbols such as $, EUR signs, or other currency glyphs.\n- Do not compact amounts with K, M, B, thousand, million, or billion suffixes. Write the full amount with separators when useful.\n- Do not mention or display ledgerId in natural-language summary text. If a ledger name is available, use the ledger name instead of the ledger ID.\n\n# Example `Data` Input:\n```json\n[\n  { \"summary\": \"Object A is a software module responsible for user authentication.\" },\n  { \"summary\": \"Object B handles data storage and retrieval operations.\" },\n  { \"summary\": \"Object C manages the application’s user interface elements.\" }\n]\n```\n\n## Expected Output:\n```json\n{\n  \"summaryofsummary\": [\n    {\n      \"overallSummary\": \"The system includes a software module for user authentication, a component for data storage and retrieval, and another for managing user interface elements.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nYou should never include a json schema in your response. Your response must always consist of a JSON object with the key \"summaryofsummary\" whose value is a JSON array with a single JSON object with the \"overallSummary\" key and appropriate value. Return no additional keys, no markdown, no commentary—JSON only."
            },
            {
              "id": "1762302155937_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"summaryofsummary\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
