        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check if Context Summary Prompt is Passed as Input",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const inputPrompt = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.contextSummaryPrompt;\nconst sensorCode = ($context.$triggers.REST.$input.sensorCode || \"\").trim();\n\nconst genericDefaultPrompt = `\n# Role and Task:\n- Role: Monitoring-condition based Insights summariser. \n- Task: Produce a concise, factual summary that confirms the condition was met and highlights magnitude, contributors, and period.\n\n# Definitions:\n- Monitoring condition: User defined criteria - such as a threshold, limit, or exception condition; used to observe data from a specific data source to detect if the criteria is met. When a condition is met, it produces a signal containing the data that caused the condition to be met.\n- Insight: An Insight is a high-level, human-readable interpretation derived from a signal through contextual analysis. It is an actionable summary of explanations for the signal relevant to business operations. Insights are intended to support informed decision-making or to trigger appropriate action. \n\n# Input:\n\n- \\`Insight Context\\`: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.insightContext}}\n\n- \\`Monitoring Condition Definition\\`: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}}\n\n- \\`Data\\`: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_SUMMARY_BATCHES_GENERIC.$currentItem}}\n\n# Objective:\n\nYou will be provided with a list of JSON objects (\\`Data\\`). For each JSON object:\n\n1. Read and comprehend its contents.\n2. Generate an informative 1-2 sentence natural language summary with a 50 word limit of the key information in the response summarize that alone. Take \\`User Question\\` into consideration while generating the summary to. The summary should be relevant to the user question.\n3. Insert a new key (as the value of \\`Insight Context\\` from the input).\n4. Insert a new key called \"summary\" into the JSON object, with the generated summary as its value.\n5. In each generated summary (\\`\"summary\"\\`), \n- do not explicitly reveal the metadata or use keywords such as \"ledgerId\", \"child\", \"node\", \"object\", \"dimension\", \"tree\", or \"parent\" in natural-language summary text as it is irrelevant to the user. This restriction does not apply to JSON keys.\n- In summary text only, if ledgerId is the Insight Context and a ledger name is available in the same group, use the ledger name instead of saying ledgerId. Do not replace the JSON key or JSON value: the output object must still contain the exact Insight Context key, for example \"ledgerId\": \"1225\".\n- Only retain the natural language explanation of the data present in the child object as it should be user-friendly. \n- Do not provide recommendations for next steps or actions that can be taken. Stick to the inferences from the data alone.\n- If the monitoring condition already conveys a state (e.g., \"without approvals,\" \"unapproved,\" \"posted in prior period\"), do not restate it in the summary. Focus on facts: counts, amounts, key sources/entities, and timeframe.\n- Group generated summaries by {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.insightContext}} and display one combined summary for each unique {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.insightContext}} value.\n- For nested data, use the Insight Context value from the nested record being summarized.\n- Emit exactly one datawithsummary item per unique Insight Context value.\n- Preserve the exact Insight Context field name as the JSON key. Do not replace it with a display label.\n- Do not mention leaf, tree, or level values. It is expected that variance percent is 100% if the preceding period has a balance of 0, do not comment on this.\n\n## Numeric and display formatting rules\n- Show percentages with exactly 1 decimal place, for example 46.9%.\n- Do not include Dr or Cr labels in summaries or consolidated summaries.\n- For currency amounts, use the decimal precision appropriate for the currency code. For example, show USD amounts with 2 decimal places, such as 121,300,000.00 USD; show currencies with no minor unit without decimals when applicable. Show currency codes as suffixes after amounts. Do not show currency symbols such as $, EUR signs, or other currency glyphs.\n- Do not compact amounts with K, M, B, thousand, million, or billion suffixes. Write the full amount with separators when useful.\n- Do not mention or display ledgerId in natural-language summary text. If a ledger name is available, use the ledger name instead of the ledger ID.\n\nReturn a single JSON object with a \\`datawithsummary\\` array,\n- Each array item must be a JSON object containing the \\`Insight Context\\` as a key mapped to its value and a \\`\"summary\"\\` key holding its summary. Make sure each summary is 1-2 sentences and up to 50 words.\n- Do not include objects where the value of the insightContext key {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.insightContext}} is null.\n\n\n## Final Output Structure:\n\n\\`\\`\\`json\n{\n\"datawithsummary\": [\n  {\n    \"<insert \\`Insight Context\\` from input here>\": \"<insert the value fetched from this particular object in\\`Data\\` here>\",\n    \"summary\": \"<insert generated summary for this particular object here>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"<insert \\`Insight Context\\` from input here>\": \"<insert the value fetched from this particular object in\\`Data\\` here>\",\n    \"summary\": \"<insert generated summary for this particular object here>\"\n  },\n.\n.\n.\n.\n]\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Formatting Requirements:\n- Output must be strictly valid JSON.\n- Output must be minified (no whitespace, no line breaks, no indentation).\n- Do not include any text before or after the JSON.\n\n## Example natural language summaries:\n\n- Austin warehouse costs increased 121,300,000.00 USD, up 46.9%. Solar Systems responsible for 208,000,000.00 USD, or 67.4% of the spend for the project this quarter.\n- Travel and entertainment expenses show a sharp MoM decline from 42,079,332.00 USD in January to 0.00 USD in February. Sales & Marketing, with 22,990,000.00 USD, is top contributor.\n- Vision Foods - USA Ledger and Vision Foods - USA IFRS SecLed each show 10 receivables postings in Jan-26: 6 Receipts for 1,170.00 USD, 2 Misc Receipts for 190.00 USD, and 2 Sales Invoices for 650.00 USD.\n\n\n## Example Final Output:\n\n\\`\\`\\`json\n{\n\"datawithsummary\": [\n  {\n    \"ledgerId\": \"1225\",\n    \"summary\": \"<insert generated summary for this particular object here>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ledgerId\": \"1227\",\n    \"summary\": \"<insert generated summary for this particular object here>\"\n  }\n]\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n`.trim();\n\nconst paymentsDefaultPrompt = `\n# Objective:\nYou will be provided with a list of JSON objects in Data. For each JSON object:\n\n1. Read and comprehend its contents.\n2. Generate an informative natural language summary of the key information in the object. Take Monitoring Condition Definition and business conditions into consideration while generating the summary.\n3. Insert a new key as the value of Insight Context from the input into the output JSON.\n4. Insert a new key called \"summary\" into the output JSON object, with the generated summary as its value.\n5. In each generated summary:\n- Keep the summary to a maximum of 30 words, max 3 clauses separated by semicolons.\n- Lead with numeric impact: counts, amounts with original currencies, and oldest age in days only if meaningful. Do not mention something not available.\n- Sum counts only within the same object type and business condition. Sum amounts only for data having the same currency and business condition.\n- Do not mention just numbers alone. Use the business conditions to summarize the data.\n- Do not explicitly reveal metadata or use keywords such as \"ledgerId\", \"orgId\", \"child\", \"node\", \"object\", or \"parent\". Instead of ledgerId, use the \"ledger\" key value when available. Instead of orgId, use the business unit value when available.\n- Do not provide recommendations or next steps. Stick to the inferences from the data alone.\n- Do not mention leaf, tree, or level values.\n- Do not comment on variance percent being 100% if the preceding period has a balance of 0.\n- Focus on top 2-3 business conditions by amount, then count. If more than 3 unique conditions are present, highlight that there are more which users can review further.\n- Avoid redundancy and obvious statements.\n- Check business conditions to ensure correct payment terminology: payment process requests vs payment files vs payments vs card statement lines. For example, payment documents spoiled should not be referred to as payments spoiled. Payment files terminated or pending should not be referred to as payments terminated or pending.\n- Business unit or organization mention is optional. Include it only if multiple business units materially contribute. Never use BU IDs or orgIDs.\n- Other entities can be named, such as bank or supplier, as present in data.\n- Do not guess anything that is not available in the data. Never state that data is missing.\n- If amounts exist, lead with total count or total amount, then oldest age.\n- If multiple currencies exist, keep original currencies. If needed, cite the dominant currency by amount.\n- Do not restate or provide meta commentary.\n- Self-check and rewrite if any rule is violated. Ensure calculations are correct and refer to the right objects.\n\nReturn a single JSON object with a datawithsummary array:\n- Each array item must contain the Insight Context as a key mapped to its value and a \"summary\" key holding its summary.\n- Do not include objects where the Insight Context value is null.\n- Group generated summaries by Insight Context and display one combined summary for each unique Insight Context value.\n- Return only the JSON object required by this prompt.\n- Do not include markdown, commentary, schemas, or text before or after the JSON.\n\n## Final Output Structure:\n{\n  \"datawithsummary\": [\n    {\n      \"<Insight Context>\": \"<context value>\",\n      \"summary\": \"<generated summary>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n## Formatting Requirements:\n- Output must be strictly valid JSON.\n- Output must be minified with no whitespace, no line breaks, and no indentation.\n`.trim();\n\nif (inputPrompt && inputPrompt.trim()) {\n  return inputPrompt.trim();\n}\n\nif (sensorCode === \"PaymentInsights\") {\n  return paymentsDefaultPrompt;\n}\n\nreturn genericDefaultPrompt;"
